	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/plain" rect="(370.0, 329.0, 737.0, 261.0)" font-family="Sans Serif" font-size="16">The Central Line (Median): It is the heart of the chart. It divides the data exactly in half. If the line is not in the center of the box, the data is “pulled” to one side (skewness).

The Box (The Body): Represents the central 50% of the data (from the 1st to the 3rd quartile). This is where the main “mass” of the information lies.

The Whiskers: Show the spread of values outside the box, indicating the expected limits of the data.

The Isolated Points (Outliers): These are the “strange” or extreme values that fall outside the whiskers. It is the fastest way to identify sensor errors or exceptional cases.</text>
	</annotations>
